        detailEn: "With the server running in the background, manually validated the full flow from different Windows terminals (PowerShell and cmd.exe): direct interactive chat with ollama run qwen2.5:3b-instruct-q4_K_M, a query against Ollama's raw API, and a query against the project's own endpoint (POST /api/chat) via curl.exe, confirming the response, sources and timing (elapsed_ms) all come back correctly outside the context of an automated script. The validation confirmed a core distinction of the project: a bare ollama run <model> has no grounding in the data/knowledge/ documents, it only answers with the model's general knowledge — it's the project's own endpoint, with its similarity search, that anchors the response to real context. It also confirmed that asking the model to describe its own parameters or training isn't reliable; for real specs, ollama show <model> or /show info is the right tool, since it reads real metadata from the model file instead of generating it.",
